$DIR/main.p:49:8: cannot take the address of a.a: it is a packed field that is not whole bytes of plain memory
    The address of a packed field can be taken only when the field is whole
    bytes of plain memory: a field declared with a type, not bits[T, N], an enum
    or a flag group, that starts on a byte, is not a bool or an array of bools,
    lies in a value that is not volatile, and holds its bytes as a variable of
    its type would. A field of several bytes in a big-endian packed type does
    not, and no field of a big-endian integer-backed type does. The rule covers
    &x.f, slicing an array field, and calling a method with a pointer receiver
    on a field.
    Copy the field to a variable, use the copy, and write it back.
    (see "packed types" in the Plutonium spec, section 7.14)
    (run "pluto explain E2112" for a longer explanation)

